    "title": "Who Won ‘The Voice’ Spring 2026? Season 29 Winner Revealed! [Spoiler]",
    "text": "The Voice has just revealed its season 29 winner! NBC’s long-running singing competition show saw four finalists going into the finale on Tuesday night (April 14), but only one of them was picked as the winner. Team Adam Levine and Team John Legend brought one act each, while Team Kelly Clarkson brought two acts. This season was also a little different than seasons past as it was “Battle of the Champions,” meaning it featured just three winning coaches and some new rules like the “Super Steal” and “Triple Turn.” The finale featured several performances throughout from the finalists and the coaches. But who actually ended up winning The Voice season 29? Keep reading to find out more… ALEXIA JAYY WINS!!! Alexia Jayy was announced as the winner!! Alexia was on Team Adam, and this marks his fourth win on the competition series. 4th place: Mikenley Brown 3rd place: Lucas West Runner up: Liv Ciara The judges were all very happy for Alexia and shared their touching thoughts with Alexia getting on the phone to her mom right after for an emotional phone call. “Oh god, this means so much, I cannot believe that I just won The Voice. I get to take this back home to my babies,” she said.",
